    "body": "This PR adds a new Spark L2 wallet backend to Nutshell. \n\nBecause Spark L2's self-custodial guarantees rely on complex FROST cryptography which is currently only officially available via their TypeScript SDK (`@buildonspark/spark-sdk`), this backend uses a \"sidecar\" architecture.\n\n### Key features:\n- **Node.js Bridge**: Added a lightweight TypeScript Express server (`cashu/lightning/sparkl2_bridge`) that wraps the Spark SDK and exposes simple REST/SSE endpoints for status, invoice creation, payments, and event streaming.\n- **Python Backend**: Added `cashu/lightning/sparkl2.py` which implements the `LightningBackend` interface and communicates with the Node.js sidecar. \n- **Auto-spawning**: The Python backend automatically spawns the Node.js bridge in the background when it is instantiated.\n- **Deterministic Keys**: The sidecar's deterministic Spark wallet seed is derived directly and securely from the mint's `MINT_PRIVATE_KEY` passed via the API at initialization. No separate key management is required.\n- **Fee parsing**: Correctly parses the `CurrencyAmount` objects from the Spark SDK for robust fee estimation and routing.\n- **Status tracking**: Accurately maps the Spark SDK status ENUM variants (e.g. `LIGHTNING_PAYMENT_RECEIVED`, `TRANSFER_COMPLETED`) to Nutshell's internal `PaymentResult` instances.\n\n### Usage\nUsers can enable the backend by setting:\n```env\nMINT_BACKEND_BOLT11_SAT=SparkL2Wallet\nMINT_SPARK_NETWORK=TESTNET # or MAINNET\n```\n",
